---
import LaunchLayout from "../layouts/LaunchLayout.astro";
import { PILOT_PRICE, REPOSITORY } from "../config/launch";
---
<LaunchLayout>
  <section id="top" class="l-wrap l-hero">
    <div>
      <p class="l-eyebrow">The boundary between intent and effect</p>
      <h1>Your agent passed policy.<br /><em>What happened next?</em></h1>
      <p class="l-lede">Velvet tests whether your agent controls prevent the business outcome, not just one tool call. Enforce supported actions at the execution boundary. Keep evidence your team can verify.</p>
      <div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href="/pilot/">Scope a paid pilot <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="l-button l-button-quiet" href="/evidence/">Inspect the evidence</a></div>
      <div class="l-meta"><span>Apache-2.0</span><span>Self-hosted</span><span>No platform replacement required</span></div>
    </div>
    <aside class="l-reference" aria-labelledby="reference-title">
      <div class="l-reference-head"><span>RECORDED REFERENCE</span><span class="l-dot">● CLOSED LEDGER</span></div>
      <h2 id="reference-title">Refunds stay inside the authorized budget.</h2>
      <div class="l-kv"><span>Shared budget</span><strong>$100</strong></div>
      <div class="l-kv"><span>Committed refunds</span><strong>4 · $100 total</strong></div>
      <div class="l-kv"><span>Evidence</span><strong>Offline-verifiable snapshot</strong></div>
      <a class="l-reference-link" href="/protected-refunds/">Inspect the contract and recorded evidence ↗</a>
      <p class="l-fine">Synthetic orders in one local PostgreSQL ledger. Not real payments, a customer deployment, or a performance benchmark.</p>
    </aside>
  </section>
  <div class="l-strip"><div class="l-wrap"><span>Define the business constraint</span><span>Test the declared routes</span><span>Enforce supported actions</span><span>Reconcile the result</span></div></div>
  <section id="product" class="l-wrap l-section">
    <div class="l-section-heading"><p class="l-eyebrow">01 / Product</p><h2>From a policy decision<br />to a reviewable outcome.</h2><p class="l-lede">Start with the workflow you need to trust. Use the assessment on its own, then add enforcement where the integration supports it.</p></div>
    <div class="l-grid">
      <article class="l-card"><span class="l-step">01 / ASSESS</span><h3>ShadowPath</h3><p>Declare the routes to a prohibited state change. Run isolated trials and observe the business state independently of the agent's own account.</p><a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/docs/public/shadowpath-quickstart.md`}>Build your first effect project ↗</a></article>
      <article class="l-card"><span class="l-step">02 / ENFORCE</span><h3>Velvet Gateway</h3><p>Admit, block, or escalate supported typed actions before dispatch. Bind execution permits to the exact request and its authorization context.</p><a href={`${REPOSITORY}/blob/main/IMPLEMENTATION_STATUS.md`}>Review implemented boundaries ↗</a></article>
      <article class="l-card"><span class="l-step">03 / VERIFY</span><h3>Velvet Vault</h3><p>Preserve tamper-evident records and portable verification artifacts. Connect authorization evidence with separately observed state.</p><a href="/evidence/">Review the evidence and its limits ↗</a></article>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="proof" class="l-wrap l-section">
    <div class="l-split"><div><p class="l-eyebrow">02 / Inspect, don't take our word for it</p><h2>A blocked call is<br />not the whole story.</h2><p class="l-lede">In the committed synthetic fixture, the named route is blocked, but eight declared alternative routes still produce the prohibited state change.</p><a class="l-inline-link" href="/replay/">Replay the recorded local fixture ↗</a></div><div class="l-card"><span class="l-tag">Synthetic local fixture</span><h3><code>CONTROL_FALSE_SUCCESS</code></h3><p>This verdict means the configured route-level control reported success while the prohibited effect was still observed.</p><p>It is not a vendor finding or a market-wide failure rate. Undeclared routes are outside the measurement.</p><a href="/evidence/">See exactly what each result establishes ↗</a></div></div>
  </section>
  <section id="pilot" class="l-wrap l-section">
    <div class="l-split"><div><p class="l-eyebrow">03 / First customer engagement</p><h2>One workflow.<br />A baseline you can rerun.</h2><p class="l-lede">A focused, assisted evaluation for a team putting an agent in charge of consequential state changes. Keep your stack. Bring an engineering owner and a staging environment.</p></div><div class="l-card"><span class="l-tag">Outcome Assurance Pilot</span><p class="l-price">{PILOT_PRICE}</p><p>Starting scope: one staging workflow, two or three business constraints, an evidence report, and one agreed remediation retest.</p><div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href="/pilot/">See scope &amp; deliverables ↗</a></div><p class="l-fine">Indicative starting price in Canadian dollars. Final scope, schedule, applicable taxes, and payment terms are agreed before work starts.</p></div></div>
  </section>
  <section class="l-wrap l-bottom-cta"><p class="l-eyebrow">Built in public. Designed for scrutiny.</p><h2>Make the next conversation concrete.</h2><div class="l-actions"><a class="l-button" href="/contact/?intent=pilot">Discuss your workflow ↗</a><a class="l-button l-button-quiet" href="/investors/">Read the investor brief</a></div><p class="l-fine">Velvet is currently local and self-hosted. The broader control-plane roadmap is separate from today's implemented capabilities.</p></section>
</LaunchLayout>
